          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP636 CBP4 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another nice walk in the park. We did better than the people walking across the river, the south side pathway is still an ice flow! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Outforthehunt for maintaining the Brass Cap cache for everyone to enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682506085">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP636 - CBP4&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I managed to convince One Bad Ant that with the impending doom.... er, I mean, the upcoming change in logging rules, that we should do a multi-day blitzing of Brass Caps! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; This was enough of a walk to get the furry cacher out again! We had some fun too... I started chasing her around a little bit! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; She seemed to have fun! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Then we got to the cap and it was time to get back to business... her finding sticks and things to chew and eat, and me taking pictures of things in the ground. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; It wasn't obvious at first, but then I found the right divet! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; It's a bit scratched up, but not too bad. TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
